WEBVTT

00:01.880 --> 00:05.720
This world is filled with
too many games to count,

00:06.980 --> 00:11.290
though the vast majority simply
come and go in obscurity.

00:12.610 --> 00:15.400
The greatest of all games

00:15.400 --> 00:20.740
is the fully immersive VR game boasting
over 30 million players worldwide—

00:20.740 --> 00:25.290
Shangri-La Frontier<i>, which rightly
earns the title of "god-tier game"!</i>

00:27.000 --> 00:30.920
One lover of trash games, Rakuro Hizutome,

00:30.920 --> 00:34.140
is trying out the god-tier
game, Shangri-La Frontier<i>!</i>

00:34.930 --> 00:39.650
What adventures await him there?

02:11.670 --> 02:12.830
I've verified what I needed to,

02:12.830 --> 02:15.050
so here's the plan!

02:17.180 --> 02:18.800
Ignore the scrubs!

02:18.800 --> 02:20.770
Straight to the area boss!

02:20.770 --> 02:21.410
That is all!

02:24.070 --> 02:24.990
Get on my shoulder!

02:24.990 --> 02:26.190
Righty-o!

02:40.950 --> 02:44.370
A characteristic of Shangri-La
Frontier<i>'s "swamp" terrain</i>

02:45.640 --> 02:48.810
is that it forces a "walking state."

02:48.810 --> 02:52.190
One leg always remains trapped in the marsh

02:52.190 --> 02:54.230
until the other foot reaches the bottom.

02:56.610 --> 02:57.690
Rec. Party Size: 4
<b>Area Boss
Mud Digger</b>

02:57.690 --> 02:58.650
In other words...
Rec. Party Size: 4
<b>Area Boss
Mud Digger</b>

02:58.650 --> 02:59.030
Rec. Party Size: 4
<b>Area Boss
Mud Digger</b>

03:00.140 --> 03:04.140
This is my worst match-up possible!

03:06.680 --> 03:10.830
Lo, Thou Art Assailed on All Sides

03:16.330 --> 03:21.120
How am I gonna fight with the
swamp locking down my speed?

03:26.990 --> 03:29.550
How does he dive into mud that shallow?

03:30.110 --> 03:31.840
Well, I guess that's game logic for you...

03:32.320 --> 03:34.230
He's on the way, Sunraku-san!

03:34.570 --> 03:38.100
Oh, it's going to skin us alive!

03:38.100 --> 03:39.860
What are you, the Hare of Inaba?

03:44.500 --> 03:45.700
Hang on tight, Emul!

03:45.950 --> 03:46.910
Righty-o!

03:49.250 --> 03:50.330
Slide Move

03:51.160 --> 03:52.710
Slide Move!

03:54.170 --> 03:57.090
<b>Slide Move
</b>Evades an attack with a gliding motion.

04:00.350 --> 04:05.260
The EXP from the Lycagon battle
evolved a bunch of my skills.

04:05.260 --> 04:06.640
Figuring out how to use them

04:07.320 --> 04:08.600
will be the key to this battle!

04:18.160 --> 04:21.280
An evolution of Perfect Parry...

04:22.920 --> 04:23.590
<b>Repel Counter</b>

04:23.590 --> 04:25.110
Repel Counter!
<b>Repel Counter</b>

04:25.110 --> 04:28.200
<b>Repel Counter
</b>Parries one incoming attack
and unleashes a counterattack.

04:31.130 --> 04:33.180
Truly impressive, Sunraku-san!

04:33.180 --> 04:35.730
I just used some skills to
get out of a tight spot.

04:35.730 --> 04:37.000
I still haven't addressed the real challenge.

04:38.350 --> 04:39.760
Just seconds into the battle and

04:39.760 --> 04:42.890
I've already used both the skills that
seemed useful for damage evasion.

04:43.510 --> 04:44.390
Slide Move
Repel Counter

04:44.390 --> 04:46.060
The recast time is ten seconds.
Slide Move
Repel Counter

04:46.060 --> 04:46.840
Slide Move
Repel Counter

04:49.240 --> 04:51.840
I've got no way to avoid
damage in the meantime.

04:52.270 --> 04:53.310
What do I do?

05:11.950 --> 05:13.620
Magic Edge!

05:23.630 --> 05:25.470
Oh, I succeeded!

05:25.470 --> 05:28.170
Hey, what was that? Magic?

05:28.170 --> 05:30.510
Yes, indeed, it was!

05:30.880 --> 05:32.380
<i>Of course.</i>

05:32.380 --> 05:35.200
<i>I'd been so focused on soloing this game,</i>

05:35.200 --> 05:36.890
<i>I forgot I've got a partner.</i>

05:37.690 --> 05:42.840
<i>Seems sorta iffy for a real gamer to
be relying on a stronger NPC, but...</i>

05:42.840 --> 05:46.900
<i>She gave me this chance,
so I'm not gonna waste it!</i>

05:47.580 --> 05:48.710
Let's go, Emul!

05:48.710 --> 05:50.320
Let's close the distance with
Accel while it's still reeling!

05:50.320 --> 05:51.510
<b>Accel
</b>Grants a temporary bonus to
attack power and agility.
Let's close the distance with
Accel while it's still reeling!

05:51.510 --> 05:52.280
<b>Accel
</b>Grants a temporary bonus to
attack power and agility.

05:52.660 --> 05:56.010
Yes! Yes! Yes! Yes!

05:56.010 --> 05:57.370
Yes! Yes!

05:57.370 --> 05:59.330
This freaking sucks!

06:08.860 --> 06:10.140
And now...

06:12.460 --> 06:14.350
The evolution of Screw Pierce...

06:15.200 --> 06:15.850
<b>Spiral
Edge</b>

06:15.850 --> 06:17.620
Spiral Edge!
<b>Spiral
Edge</b>

06:23.870 --> 06:24.940
Now, keeping up the pressure!

06:26.020 --> 06:27.320
Edge Climb!

06:27.320 --> 06:27.990
<b>Edge Climb
</b>Stick a bladed weapon into
a vertical service to climb.
Edge Climb!

06:27.990 --> 06:29.280
<b>Edge Climb
</b>Stick a bladed weapon into
a vertical service to climb.

06:34.050 --> 06:34.950
There!

06:35.270 --> 06:35.990
Emul!

06:35.990 --> 06:37.030
Yes?!

06:37.030 --> 06:38.460
How about giving us a big boom?

06:38.460 --> 06:39.410
I...

06:39.410 --> 06:41.710
I certainly shall!

06:41.710 --> 06:43.250
Add Spell!

06:43.250 --> 06:43.270
<b>Add Spell
Add Spell!</b>

06:43.270 --> 06:44.210
<b>Add Spell</b>

06:44.520 --> 06:46.910
Hup! Hoi! Whoops!

06:46.910 --> 06:50.650
I've played trash games with
trickier platforming than this!

06:50.650 --> 06:52.720
Go on and eat me if you can!

06:59.480 --> 07:01.980
Too late. It's been ten seconds.

07:02.230 --> 07:02.530
<b>Repel Counter</b>

07:02.530 --> 07:04.480
Repel Counter!
<b>Repel Counter</b>

07:08.990 --> 07:10.860
Here comes the big boom!

07:10.860 --> 07:14.120
Power-Boost Magic Edge!

07:16.760 --> 07:18.000
<b><i>Power-Boost Magic Edge</i></b>

07:18.420 --> 07:20.160
Hell yeah!

07:27.070 --> 07:27.190
<b><i>Sunraku</i></b>

07:27.190 --> 07:27.900
<b>Fall Damage -8
<i>Sunraku</i></b>

07:27.900 --> 07:29.050
<b><i>Sunraku</i></b>

07:29.530 --> 07:31.220
That was perfect, Emul!

07:31.220 --> 07:32.250
Nice shot!

07:32.250 --> 07:35.190
Oh, dear! My poor clothing!

07:35.190 --> 07:37.140
That spell really packed a wallop.

07:37.140 --> 07:38.270
It's gotta be—

07:38.560 --> 07:39.340
Eh?

07:39.340 --> 07:41.440
Where'd he get off to?

07:50.690 --> 07:53.440
What's with all the shaking?

07:53.440 --> 07:56.240
It's like it's sucking my
feet down. I can't move!

07:56.240 --> 07:58.240
Sunraku-san, this is...

07:59.500 --> 08:02.620
It rockets out of the ground to attack,

08:02.620 --> 08:05.000
so it's crucial to find a
way to hold it in place!

08:17.050 --> 08:20.720
Sunraku-san?!

08:21.370 --> 08:22.980
<i>It threw me into the air?!</i>

08:25.610 --> 08:27.730
<i>I figured that'd be an insta-kill attack,
but it barely did any damage?</i>

08:27.730 --> 08:29.610
<b><i>Sunraku
I figured that'd be an insta-kill attack,
but it barely did any damage?</i></b>

08:35.610 --> 08:36.460
<i>No, wait.</i>

08:36.460 --> 08:37.870
<i>From this height...</i>

08:38.470 --> 08:42.120
The Mud Digger is a mole-like
quadruped with the

08:42.120 --> 08:45.060
head of a shark and the
whiskers of a catfish.

08:45.550 --> 08:49.710
Its most noteworthy trait is the special
move set that activates after its HP

08:49.710 --> 08:51.380
reach a certain threshold.

08:52.350 --> 08:58.220
It dives deep into the ground and vibrates
the swamp to hold players in place.

08:58.850 --> 09:02.490
Then it randomly rams one of them
up in the air with its nose.

09:03.020 --> 09:05.020
If a player challenges it alone,

09:05.020 --> 09:06.460
not only will it hit them
with this attack every time

09:06.460 --> 09:08.490
as long as they remain in the swamp,

09:08.490 --> 09:13.290
but it will almost inevitably shave down
all their HP through fall damage,

09:13.290 --> 09:16.300
hence its sobriquet—the "solo killer."

09:16.300 --> 09:18.030
<i>It's gonna kill me through falling damage?</i>

09:18.030 --> 09:22.330
<i>And since the initial juggle
attack not doing much damage...</i>

09:22.820 --> 09:26.460
<i>Whoever came up with this boss
has a real nasty personality!</i>

09:26.700 --> 09:28.970
<i>Player skill's not even
a factor at this point!</i>

09:28.970 --> 09:30.710
<i>What do I do?!</i>

09:33.160 --> 09:36.040
<i>If Emul hit me from the
side with her Magic Edge...</i>

09:36.040 --> 09:37.930
<i>No, that'd just blow me up!</i>

09:38.390 --> 09:42.150
<i>Magic, items... anything I can do?!</i>

09:42.680 --> 09:44.510
<i>Nah, I'm done for.</i>

09:44.510 --> 09:45.520
<i>I'm totally screwed.</i>

09:45.880 --> 09:49.520
<i>I've never been able to get used
to falling deaths in VR games.</i>

09:51.370 --> 09:54.310
<i>A feeling of electricity
running through your body,</i>

09:54.310 --> 09:56.650
<i>followed by a total loss of feeling...</i>

09:57.400 --> 10:03.220
<i>The unnecessary pursuit of reality resulted
in some games to be taken off the market.</i>

10:05.160 --> 10:08.970
Show your vorpal spirit!

10:10.000 --> 10:10.960
<b>Magic Scroll
Teleport</b>

10:19.220 --> 10:24.470
There's an attack skill called
"Meteor Fall" that utilizes downward energy.

10:24.470 --> 10:24.960
<b>Meteor Fall
Energy</b>

10:24.960 --> 10:28.230
Sunraku, had picked up a lot of
downward momentum from his free fall
<b>Meteor Fall
Energy</b>

10:28.230 --> 10:28.550
<b>Energy</b>

10:28.550 --> 10:30.750
at which point, Emul teleported
him over the Mud Digger.
<b>Energy</b>

10:30.750 --> 10:31.750
at which point, Emul teleported
him over the Mud Digger.

10:31.750 --> 10:31.890
<b>Energy
at which point, Emul teleported
him over the Mud Digger.</b>

10:31.890 --> 10:32.810
<b>Energy</b>

10:32.810 --> 10:35.940
An attack that might normally be deemed
a fall and result in player death,

10:36.330 --> 10:40.920
was, in a slipshod way,
recognized instead as a risky attack.

10:41.270 --> 10:41.530
It was not Meteor Fall,

10:41.530 --> 10:42.960
<b>Mistake
Meteor Fall
It was not Meteor Fall,</b>

10:42.960 --> 10:45.240
but Mistake Meteor Fall!
<b>Mistake
Meteor Fall</b>

11:00.430 --> 11:01.290
<b><i>Sunraku</i></b>

11:01.290 --> 11:03.180
Did I seriously survive that?!
<b><i>Sunraku</i></b>

11:03.180 --> 11:03.200
Did I seriously survive that?!

11:05.210 --> 11:07.810
Splendidly done, Sunraku-san!

11:08.520 --> 11:10.770
So many things happened all at once,

11:10.770 --> 11:13.290
I'm having a hard time
getting it all straight...

11:13.290 --> 11:14.820
But either way, Emul...

11:15.080 --> 11:17.030
You're simply splendid!

11:17.030 --> 11:20.450
K-Kindly do not imitate my speech!

11:21.680 --> 11:25.740
Just like with Lycagon,
I had a pretty rough ride there...

11:28.110 --> 11:30.380
But we were the survivors this time!

11:32.000 --> 11:33.520
<b></b>Area Boss
<b>Mud Digger</b>

11:33.520 --> 11:37.000
<b>Dispatch Complete
</b>Area Boss
<b>Mud Digger</b>

11:50.270 --> 11:50.410
<b><i>Sunraku</i></b>

11:50.410 --> 11:51.120
<b>Herbs used.
<i>Sunraku</i></b>

11:51.120 --> 11:51.610
<b><i>Sunraku</i></b>

11:51.610 --> 11:54.520
Not even herbs'll get me back
to max HP right away, huh?
<b><i>Sunraku</i></b>

11:54.520 --> 11:56.580
Not even herbs'll get me back
to max HP right away, huh?

11:56.580 --> 11:58.880
You shoved them down your throat!

11:58.880 --> 12:02.030
That's the only way they reach my mouth.

12:02.680 --> 12:06.280
<i>Still, Emul was way stronger than I expected.</i>

12:06.840 --> 12:09.830
<i>She ended up carrying me.</i>

12:09.830 --> 12:12.540
<i>Feels pretty bad after how cocky I was...</i>

12:12.920 --> 12:17.420
<i>Until I reach Emul's level,
I'll just put her to work as a mascot.</i>

12:18.330 --> 12:20.640
<i>Might be the only way to stay motivated.</i>

12:21.320 --> 12:23.540
We'll arrive at Thirdrema soon!

12:23.540 --> 12:28.510
And after we arrive, you'll be
staying in Rabituza full-time, yes?

12:28.510 --> 12:30.060
I can hardly wait!

12:30.060 --> 12:35.250
Yeah, but there's still a question.
How do I hide you once we get into town?

12:35.250 --> 12:39.190
Drawing more attention like last
time might even get us jumped.

12:40.080 --> 12:41.570
In that case...

12:42.160 --> 12:44.390
Why, I haven't used it in so long!

12:44.970 --> 12:45.700
Used what?

12:48.120 --> 12:50.240
<b>Mysterious Vorpal Bracelet</b>

12:50.650 --> 12:54.260
The secret treasure of the Vorpal Bunnies!

12:54.260 --> 12:57.640
Sunraku-san, I must ask you
to keep this between us!

12:58.260 --> 12:59.130
Sure?

13:00.090 --> 13:01.630
Metamorphose!

13:13.210 --> 13:15.070
Surprised, are you?

13:15.070 --> 13:18.810
This will allow us to
inconspicuously enter the town!

13:21.840 --> 13:23.320
<i>Now, isn't that weird?</i>

13:23.320 --> 13:26.070
<i>Here I thought I was playing
Japan's flagship god-tier game—</i>

13:26.470 --> 13:30.580
<i>catchphrase, "Explore the
world, enjoy the world"—</i>

13:30.580 --> 13:33.610
Shangri-La Frontier<i>.</i>

13:34.190 --> 13:35.580
Sunraku-san?

13:35.910 --> 13:37.210
<i>But this is...</i>

13:37.540 --> 13:38.980
Sunraku-san?

13:38.980 --> 13:41.540
<i>This is starting to look like...</i>

13:41.540 --> 13:44.930
Sunraku-san!

13:44.930 --> 13:46.320
Hey, hey!

13:46.320 --> 13:47.690
Sunraku-san?

13:47.690 --> 13:49.850
Sunraku-san!

13:49.850 --> 13:53.100
<i>...some kind of harem game
with an anthro bunny girl!</i>

14:00.480 --> 14:01.550
Eh?

14:01.900 --> 14:03.790
It's simply so exhausting.

14:03.790 --> 14:06.700
I'll transform again once we near the town.

14:06.700 --> 14:09.930
Four or five minutes is my
limit in my current state.

14:10.490 --> 14:12.200
Oh, I get it.

14:12.200 --> 14:16.330
So once we're in town you'll have
to undo it once we're in private.

14:16.560 --> 14:20.660
But, Emil, you have committed a fatal...

14:20.660 --> 14:23.720
Yes, one truly fatal,

14:23.720 --> 14:26.090
vorpal-class failure of understanding.

14:27.510 --> 14:30.070
The minute you started hanging
out with a half-naked bird-man,

14:30.070 --> 14:31.850
you maxed out your "conspicuous" stat.

14:37.550 --> 14:39.950
Well, you'll just have to play

14:39.950 --> 14:43.930
the hapless girl dragging along a
half-naked bird-man for some reason.

14:43.930 --> 14:44.840
Good luck!

14:44.840 --> 14:48.330
My steps feel as heavy as if
I were still in the marsh.

15:02.000 --> 15:06.670
<b>Thirdrema</b>

15:06.880 --> 15:11.470
Oh, it's as large and lovely
a town as I remember!

15:11.470 --> 15:14.430
So that's Thirdrema, eh?

15:14.770 --> 15:17.820
You seem curiously unimpressed, Sunraku-san!

15:17.820 --> 15:21.410
Well, I'm not exactly a
warrior guided by destiny,

15:21.410 --> 15:24.650
but I've seen a few places in my time.

15:24.650 --> 15:25.900
How truly spectacular!

15:25.900 --> 15:29.440
You pioneers really are a well traveled lot!

15:29.440 --> 15:31.620
Okay, let's go, Emul!

15:31.620 --> 15:34.900
Get ready to transform and
make yourself inconspicuous!

15:34.900 --> 15:35.950
Righty-o!

15:41.700 --> 15:42.960
Hang on a minute!

15:42.960 --> 15:44.600
Why are you half-naked?

15:44.600 --> 15:46.460
Were you beset by highwaymen?

15:46.670 --> 15:47.700
<i>Yep, knew it.</i>

15:47.700 --> 15:50.130
<i>I'm still the conspicuous one.</i>

15:50.510 --> 15:53.210
And what frightening marks you bear...

15:53.210 --> 15:54.760
They're on his legs, too.

15:54.760 --> 15:57.260
Wait just one moment now, Mr. Guard!

15:57.940 --> 15:59.390
This man has a past...

15:59.390 --> 16:03.820
A past that would bring
sorrow to all who hear it!

16:05.810 --> 16:07.960
Guided by destiny itself,

16:07.960 --> 16:10.280
he was reborn as a super warrior,

16:10.280 --> 16:14.960
and challenged his destined rival
from his past life and this one,

16:14.960 --> 16:16.700
Lycagon, to a duel!

16:16.700 --> 16:20.000
But by the narrowest of margins,
by a mere hair's breadth,

16:20.000 --> 16:22.960
by the smallest and simplest
of fate's own whims,

16:22.960 --> 16:26.710
he ended up inflicted by a curse instead!

16:27.010 --> 16:29.710
Where'd you pull that story from?

16:29.710 --> 16:34.300
But unable to escape his destiny,
he leaves himself to the currents of fate,

16:34.300 --> 16:41.730
a solitary warrior on a wandering journey
to remove the curse that afflicts him!

16:41.730 --> 16:45.210
That is he... Sunraku-san!

16:45.210 --> 16:46.290
Hey, hang on!

16:46.290 --> 16:46.980
You—

16:46.980 --> 16:51.650
The tale of Super Warrior Sunraku has
only just entered its second season!

16:51.650 --> 16:52.590
But—

16:52.590 --> 16:54.400
Next episode is "Super Warrior Sunraku—

16:54.400 --> 16:57.490
Where the Wind Blows, Where
the Carrot Greens Waver"!

16:57.490 --> 16:59.890
F-Fine, I get it.

16:59.890 --> 17:02.320
It's unusual to see a half-naked pioneer,

17:02.320 --> 17:04.170
but not completely unheard of.

17:04.170 --> 17:05.250
You may pass.

17:06.410 --> 17:07.880
Hey. That guy...

17:08.220 --> 17:09.380
Yeah.

17:10.070 --> 17:11.370
<i>Did I just imagine it?</i>

17:11.370 --> 17:14.880
<i>That wasn't the usual "what a weirdo" vibe...</i>

17:14.880 --> 17:17.360
Shall we, then, Sunraku-san?

17:17.360 --> 17:18.600
S-Sure.

17:22.180 --> 17:23.920
I recognize you.

17:23.920 --> 17:25.480
You're Sunraku, right?

17:25.900 --> 17:28.150
Um...

17:29.500 --> 17:31.000
And who might you be again?

17:32.900 --> 17:34.490
<b>Several Hours Earlier - Secondale</b>

17:34.890 --> 17:36.150
Wait!

17:36.700 --> 17:41.160
Aw, I wanted to know how you tame them!

17:42.120 --> 17:42.850
File Saved

17:42.850 --> 17:45.910
I got a screenshot!
Let's ask on the forums!
File Saved

17:46.220 --> 17:47.330
Great idea!

17:47.330 --> 17:50.210
I bet the more advanced
players know all about it!

17:50.210 --> 17:51.730
Let's see...

17:51.730 --> 17:55.150
"I have a question for our esteemed elders.

17:55.150 --> 18:00.220
I was picking up equipment in Secondale
when I ran into this player.

18:00.610 --> 18:03.740
He had the cutest talking bunny with him.

18:03.740 --> 18:07.000
How can I befriend this monster?"

18:07.000 --> 18:08.940
And send!

